    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0147" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1940</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs at Nanking to
                        the Chinese Legation</hi><anchor n="41a" xml:id="d41-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-22">September 22, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Today’s Rengo report from Tokyo stating that the Japanese Government has decided
                    to accept the Chinese Government’s formal proposal for the formation of a
                    Sino-Japanese Joint Investigation Committee is not true.</p>
                <p>The Chinese Government has never made such a proposal, formal or informal.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d41-f1" n="41a" type="source" xml:id="d41-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram handed by the Chinese Chargé to Mr. Ransford S. Miller of the
                    Division of Far Eastern Affairs, September 23.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
